0 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407770 1071 "Let $a=-53$ and $n=7.$ Find integers $q$ and $r$ such that $a=qn+r,$ where $0\\le r<n.$ Then, $r=$" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407770 1072 #uuid "411dd7b8-effc-5fa5-873f-f9e9d66680ce" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407770 1074 "Dividing $-53$ by $7$ using integer division, we notice that\n\n$$\n-8<-53÷7<-7.\n$$\n\nThe quotient $q$ is the left-hand value. So $q=-8.$\n\nNext, we find the remainder $r$ by solving $r=a-qn.$ This gives\n\n$$\nr=-53-(-8)(7)=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write $-53=qn+r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-53={{(-8)}_{⏟}}_{q}\\cdot 7+{{3}_{⏟}}_{r}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $r=3.$" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407771 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407767 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407771 1069 "q-79910" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407771 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407771 1071 "Let $a=96$ and $n=7.$ Find positive integers $q$ and $r$ such that $a=qn+r,$ where $0\\le r<n,$ and determine $q\\cdot r.$" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407771 1072 #uuid "4190f22f-14a3-5ec1-bdc7-02c4f951d26e" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407771 1074 "Dividing $96$ by $7$ using integer division, we notice that\n\n$$\n13<96÷7<14.\n$$\n\nThe quotient $q$ is the left-hand value. So $q=13.$\n\nNext, we find the remainder $r$ by computing $r=a-qn.$ This gives\n\n$$\nr=96-(13)(7)=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write $96=qn+r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}96={{13}_{⏟}}_{q}\\cdot 7+{{5}_{⏟}}_{r}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $q\\cdot r=13\\cdot 5=65.$" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407772 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407765 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407772 1069 "q-79907" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407772 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407772 1071 "Let $a=83$ and $n=6.$ Find integers $q$ and $r$ such that $a=qn+r,$ where $0\\le r<n.$ Then, $r=$" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407772 1072 #uuid "5b3d670b-6c15-5f96-828d-2a33d12d5846" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407772 1074 "Dividing $83$ by $6$ using integer division, we notice that\n\n$$\n13<83÷6<14.\n$$\n\nThe quotient $q$ is the left-hand value. So $q=13.$\n\nNext, we find the remainder $r$ by computing $r=a-qn.$ This gives\n\n$$\nr=83-(13)(6)=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write $83=qn+r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}83={{13}_{⏟}}_{q}\\cdot 6+{{5}_{⏟}}_{r}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $r=5.$" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407773 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407764 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407773 1069 "q-79914" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407773 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407773 1071 "Let $a=-63$ and $n=5.$ Find integers $q$ and $r$ such that $a=qn+r,$ where $0\\le r<n,$ and determine $q\\cdot r.$" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407773 1072 #uuid "661f54e0-10c4-53e1-98b9-3627d5f43a3c" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407773 1074 "Dividing $-63$ by $5$ using integer division, we notice that\n\n$$\n-13<-63÷5<-12.\n$$\n\nThe quotient $q$ is the left-hand value. So $q=-13.$\n\nNext, we find the remainder $r$ by solving $r=a-qn.$ This gives\n\n$$\nr=-63-(-13)(5)=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write $-63=qn+r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-63={{(-13)}_{⏟}}_{q}\\cdot 5+{{2}_{⏟}}_{r}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $q\\cdot r=-13\\cdot 2=-26.$" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407774 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407759 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407774 1069 "q-79916" 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407774 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533550 17592186045585 true] [17592186407774 1071 "Let $a=-47$ and $n=6.$ Find integers $q$ and $r$ such that $a=qn+r,$ where $0\\le r<n,$